      "writtenOn": "2026-10-30T17:40:33Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This loop unconditionally marks every redirected slice in the window—including non-faulting sibling slices (`ptep !\u003d vmf-\u003epte`)—as young (`pte_sw_mkyoung`) and dirty (`pte_mkdirty`). Unlike `p3s_swapin_map_sibling_slices()` in aosp/4379310, a write fault on a single 4KB slice will mark untouched sibling 4KB slices as accessed and dirty (`PTE_AF` and `PTE_DIRTY`) and lose/bypass per-slice `pte_soft_dirty(ptent)` / `pte_needs_soft_dirty_wp(vma, entry)` state.\n\nOnly the faulting slice (`ptep \u003d\u003d vmf-\u003epte`) should be forced young and dirty; non-faulting sibling slices (`ptep !\u003d vmf-\u003epte`) should preserve `pte_young(ptent)`, `pte_dirty(ptent)`, and `pte_soft_dirty(ptent)` from `ptent` (and only call `maybe_mkwrite(entry, vma)` when `!pte_needs_soft_dirty_wp(vma, entry)`).",
      "isAi": true,
      "revId": "55462d5316cf57e47f27ebb7fae1946ca8903bdc",
